    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and all tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to return `contactPreference = 'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`, exposed on the owner read model (`GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `contactPreference` backed by a `toContactPreference(Owner)` helper that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-blank email and `\"PHONE\"` otherwise \u2014 mirroring the existing derived-field pattern (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.).\n\nThe mapper feeds `RespondWithOwner`, which is the responder for the GET pipeline, so the field is populated on read. Both acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS.",
